Served with the launch switch on (data/boundaries.v1.json), and not before:

- The bundled boundary file. Its shapes are simplified from OpenStreetMap:
  © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database Licence 1.0
  (https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/). The file is a database
  derived from OpenStreetMap and is offered under that same licence. How it
  is made is in tools/build-boundaries.mjs.
- Its region codes were checked against Natural Earth 1:10m admin-1, version
  5.2.0-pre, which is in the public domain (https://www.naturalearthdata.com).
  No shape of Natural Earth is in the file: tried first, as the plan named it,
  it put towns such as Konstanz on the wrong side of their borders.

